Cell["The logical channel", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"66c9a615-af45-c085-0ef6-385ecaf192ef"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Encoding, applying the noise, measuring the syndrome, recovering and \
decoding is one channel on the logical qubit. Building it literally goes \
through a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["4", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0513e607-0f4c-1e20-3320-f861aaf9650a"],
 "-dimensional superoperator. But for Pauli noise on a stabilizer code the \
net result is always a logical Pauli, so the logical channel is a Pauli \
channel with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["4", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0371ff35-cd30-cda2-310e-f77ee4ca9788"],
 " weights, and those weights are exactly the coset probabilities the \
maximum-likelihood decoder already computed. So it comes out exact, symbolic, \
and cheap:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6833ae6a-6ac5-a2c8-19c0-40340f71f012"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"bitFlip", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<LogicalPauliProbabilities\>\"", ",", " ", 
